    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0216" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg204"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 (D) Regulations/9907: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Nester</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-03-09T18:00:00-04:00">March 9, 1943—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>175. Your no. 188, March 2, 2 [<hi rendition="#italic">3</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="89"
                        xml:id="d205-f1"/> In drawing up decentralization procedure, care was taken
                    to avoid regulations which would create impression that our missions are
                    invading the sovereignty of the other American republics, and for this reason,
                    the Embassy’s action was not to be indicated on copies of import recommendations
                    that got <pb facs="0217" n="205" xml:id="pg205"/> into hands of third parties.
                    If Embassy feels no repercussions likely to develop in Ecuador and in view of
                    public announcement referred to,<anchor n="90" xml:id="d205-f2"/> the Department
                    and the Board of Economic Warfare have no objection to placing action stamp on
                    fourth copy.</p>
                <p>Reference your 197, March 4, 7 p.m.<anchor n="91" xml:id="d205-f3"/></p>
                <p>The Board of Economic Warfare expects to have ready on March 11 full information
                    necessary to start operation of Plan A.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d205-f1" n="89" xml:id="d205-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d205-f2" n="90" xml:id="d205-f2-content">
                <p>The Ecuadoran Government had approved and made known to the public a procedure
                    whereby all Import Recommendations were to be the joint responsibility of the
                    Ecuadoran Office of Priorities and the American Embassy.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d205-f3" n="91" xml:id="d205-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
